  "prefLabel": "Agr 204.23 Appeal",
  "priorExpiration": "2004-07-25",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "Agr 204.23 Appeal. A final decision shall be issued before a matter can be brought on appeal. All final decisions issued by the department shall be binding, subject only to appeal to the supreme court, in accordance with RSA 541:6. However, if a division within the department has statutorily prescribed procedures regarding appeal and the issue falls within the jurisdiction of that division, the division's procedures shall prevail.\n\nSource. #6299, eff 7-25-96, EXPIRED: 7-25-04\n\nNew. #8309-A, eff 3-24-05",
  "source": "https://github.com/GraniteState/adm-rules-data/blob/1c92d82e0f03a582ca5b7a578588edf38de2318e/raw/2026-11-15/state_agencies/agr200.html"
